Privacy Policy for WebSec Auditor

Effective Date:** October 22, 2026

WebSec Auditor ("we", "our", or "app") respects your privacy.

1. Information Collection and Use
WebSec Auditor operates locally on your Android device. The application does NOT collect, store, or transmit any personal identifiable information (PII), analytics data, or device telemetry to external servers.

2. Network Requests
When you initiate an audit scan, the app performs direct network connections (HTTP/HTTPS, TLS handshakes, and DNS-over-HTTPS queries) solely to the target website or IP address specified by the user. Audit results are processed entirely on-device.

3. Local Data Storage
All scan reports and history items are stored locally in an encrypted Room database on your device. You can clear or delete your scan history at any time.

4. Contact Us
If you have questions regarding this Privacy Policy, contact us at: rselvaguru@gmail.com
